    "title": "Drone surveying in Kuwait: outputs, accuracy and planning",
    "summary": "A useful drone survey starts with the deliverable. Understand the difference between a map, a model and a measurement before commissioning your next capture.",
    "category": "Surveying & mapping",
    "author": "Orbit Aerials",
    "status": "published",
    "dateLabel": "Originally published in 2023",
    "originalDateText": "3/3/2023",
    "order": 1,
    "originalUrl": "https://www.orbitaerials.com/revolutionizing-construction-the-game-changing-benefits-of-drone-technology",
    "image": "spatial-model-preview",
    "alt": "Textured three-dimensional reconstruction of a stadium construction site with a surface-height view",
    "seoTitle": "Drone Surveying in Kuwait: Outputs & Accuracy",
    "description": "Planning a drone survey in Kuwait? Compare orthomosaics, point clouds and 3D models, and learn what to specify for accuracy, validation and delivery.",
    "published": "2023-03-03",
    "imageCaption": "Derived from Sircher’s stadium scan, CC BY 4.0. Demonstration imagery; not an Orbit project or validated survey output.",
    "takeaways": [
      "A sharp image or detailed model does not prove survey accuracy.",
      "Specify the output, reference system and acceptance criteria before capture.",
      "Use independent checks to assess the delivered result."
    ],
    "cta": "Discuss your survey requirements",
